---
/**
 * Closing CTA band. Styling lives in `.terminal .band` (global.css).
 *
 * COPY, 2026-08-16: this promised "a 30-minute working session on your live
 * accounts: where the spend is leaking… and what it is worth" — on every page
 * of the site. That is an audit of the visitor's own account plus a valuation
 * of the finding, and it is not what the demo is. `book-demo.astro` describes
 * the actual thing ("personalised walk-through of all 5 modules", "no prep
 * required before the call") and bookDemoFaqs confirms it ("we show you the
 * platform and discuss how it could work for your business").
 * The band now offers the demo we actually run, and turns "no account access"
 * from a missing promise into the objection-remover it really is.
 */
---

<section class="band" id="demo" aria-labelledby="cta-heading">
  <div class="wrap">
    <h2 id="cta-heading">Bring the whole portfolio onto one screen.</h2>
    <p>
      A 30-minute walkthrough of all five modules — the unified dashboard, how the engine paces
      budget, and the reporting owners actually read. No prep, and no access to your accounts.
    </p>
    <div class="cta-row">
      <a class="btn btn-p" href="/book-demo">Book a demo</a>
      <a class="btn btn-l" href="/pricing">Compare plans</a>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
